{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"Cross-Process Package Alignment|artifact model|review provenance|package alignment|cross-process package\" -S .'","aggregated_output":"./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:251:**Rationale:** The same artifact model should support PRDs, tech architecture\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:820:  artifact model at architectural altitude\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:643:current plan, an interstitial epic first aligns artifact model and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:38:erasing the history of work that already used them, and review provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:44:aligned artifact model where artifacts remain project-level assets and process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:148:This flow inherits Epic 5's aligned artifact model: project artifacts remain\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md:290:| TC-4.4a | mixed-producer package renders as normal package review state | User-visible package alignment |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md:421:### Chunk 4: Cross-Process Package Alignment\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:3:This epic defines the complete requirements for artifact model and review\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:89:| A6 | Source-management work in Epic 6 should inherit the aligned artifact model rather than redefine it | Validated | Platform | This epic is a prerequisite alignment step for Epic 6 |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:577:  on this aligned artifact model rather than on the prior single-primary-process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:622:cross-process package members, including the explicit package-building context\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:659:### Story 4: Cross-Process Package Alignment\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:63:durable artifact model that still leaked an older assumption: one artifact row\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:116:| Durable state | Convex behind `PlatformStore` | Platform tech arch + current repo | Keep. Artifact and package alignment remain durable-store concerns, not browser concerns |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:286:cross-process package and degraded-state coverage on top.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:458:| Chunk 4 | Cross-process package alignment and current package-building context | AC-4.1 to AC-4.4 | 23 |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:506:### Chunk 4: Cross-Process Package Alignment\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/epic.md:105:| A10 | Current artifacts shown on a process are project-level durable assets referenced by that process, and revising one in this epic creates a new version rather than transferring ownership | Validated | Platform | Epic 3 needs the aligned artifact model but not Epic 5's broader review/package behavior |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/04-cross-process-package-alignment.md:1:# Story 4: Cross-Process Package Alignment\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:41:- Story 4 cross-process package alignment\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/artifacts/04-cross-process-package-alignment/004-self-review-pass-3.json:1:{\"resultId\":\"2b6dadc8-1433-4bf1-877d-aac08bd30908\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"role\":\"story_self_review_pass\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"sessionId\":\"019dcc0f-3089-7a12-880d-209e6ed81b21\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019dcc0f-3089-7a12-880d-209e6ed81b21\",\"storyId\":\"04-cross-process-package-alignment\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"04-cross-process-package-alignment\",\"title\":\"Story 4: Cross-Process Package Alignment\"},\"passNumber\":3,\"planSummary\":\"Aligned Story 4 package publication around same-project membership plus bounded current package-building context, added automatic package-context seeding from published snapshots on reopen, and refreshed coverage so mixed-producer publish/review/export plus reopened pinned-version reuse are exercised end to end.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"reason\":\"Updated the in-memory package publication path to validate same-project members against current refs or already-pinned package-context versions, and taught package-context upsert to auto-seed from a published snapshot on reopen.\"},{\"path\":\"convex/packageSnapshots.ts\",\"reason\":\"Reworked durable package snapshot publication to allow mixed-producer members only when they belong to the same project and are valid in the publishing process’s current package-building context.\"},{\"path\":\"convex/processPackageContexts.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added durable reopen seeding so a current package context can automatically hydrate its pinned members from a published package snapshot.\"},{\"path\":\"convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Expanded package snapshot tests for mixed-producer success, cross-project rejection